---
import { Icon } from 'astro-icon/components'
import Base from '#layouts/Base.astro'
---

<Base
  title="Privacy"
  description="Data QueerOmaha.net collects, why, and who it's shared with."
>
  <article class="legal-page">
    <wa-card class="legal-card">
      <h2 slot="header">
        <Icon
          name="fa7-solid:shield-halved"
          width="1.25em"
          height="1.25em"
          aria-hidden="true"
        />
        Privacy
      </h2>

      <h3>Data Collected</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Analytics.</strong> PostHog is configured in cookieless mode and
          client IP addresses are redacted before logging.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Suggestion Box and Contact submissions.</strong> Suggestions are
          sent to Netlify and emailed to site admins. Email addresses are only used
          for correspondence and not for marketing.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Why</h3>
      <p>
        To understand which categories and listings people use, and receive
        suggestions and messages from the community.
      </p>

      <h3>Who we share it with</h3>
      <p>
        PostHog Inc. (analytics) and Netlify, Inc. (form handling and site
        hosting). We don't sell data or share it.
      </p>

      <h3>How long we keep it</h3>
      <p>
        Analytics events are kept per PostHog's standard retention. Suggestion
        Box and Contact submissions are kept until actioned and according to
        Netlify data retention.
      </p>

      <h3>Questions</h3>
      <p>
        Email <a href="mailto:privacy@queeromaha.net">privacy@queeromaha.net</a> or
        use the <a href="/contact">contact form</a>.
      </p>

      <p>
        <a class="back-link" href="/friends">
          <Icon
            name="fa7-solid:arrow-left"
            width="1.25em"
            height="1.25em"
            aria-hidden="true"
          />
          Go Back to the homepage
        </a>
      </p>
    </wa-card>
  </article>
</Base>
